<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Kendi wants a closed box whose longest straight rod, from one corner to the opposite corner, is exactly <m>{3}</m> cm. Give whole-number edge lengths for such a box.</p><div>Length <fillin characters="4" name="ans1"/> cm </div><div>Width <fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/> cm </div><div>Height <fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/> cm </div><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The rod is the space diagonal, so the edges must satisfy <m>l^2 + w^2 + h^2 = {3}^2 = {9}</m>. For example <m>{1}^2 + {2}^2 + {2}^2 = {9}</m>. All the whole-number boxes, up to order: (1, 2, 2).</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>1</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>